#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:15
msgid "Learning about data visualization - tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:18
msgid ""
"RViz is the 3D visualizer for ROS, and lets you inspect data such as shapes, "
"sensor readings, and robot models from a running system. In this tutorial, "
"you run a sample node that publishes basic shapes, then view them in RViz by "
"setting the fixed frame, adding a Marker display, and moving the camera. "
"After you follow it, you can use RViz to look at 3D data from your own ROS "
"system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:28
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:31
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:33
msgid ""
"Data visualization can be achieved by using RViz, which is a 3D visualizer "
"for ROS. RViz renders 3D data from your ROS system, such as robot models, "
"sensor readings, and primitive shapes. A display is an RViz plugin that "
"renders one kind of data in the 3D view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:37
msgid ""
"For more information, see :doc:`Visualization <../../../About-"
"visualization>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:40
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:42
msgid ""
":doc:`Install ROS <../../../../Get-Started/Installation>` and :doc:`set up "
"your environment <../../../../Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:43
msgid ""
":doc:`Create a workspace <../../../../ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-"
"with-Client-Libraries/Creating-A-Workspace/Creating-A-Workspace>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:46
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:48
msgid ""
"This tutorial uses a small publisher that cycles through a cube, sphere, "
"arrow, and cylinder. Its markers give you sample data for setup, viewing, "
"and camera control in RViz."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:52
msgid ""
"Source ROS in every new terminal you open. See :doc:`Configuring environment "
"<../../../../Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment>`. After you build the "
"tutorial package, also source your workspace overlay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:57
msgid "1 Get the marker publisher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:59
msgid ""
"This tutorial uses the ``visualization_marker_tutorials`` package from the "
"`visualization_tutorials repository <https://github.com/ros-visualization/"
"visualization_tutorials>`__. The ``basic_shapes`` executable publishes one "
"marker at a time on ``/visualization_marker``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:62
msgid ""
"Clone the repository into the ``src`` directory of your workspace, then "
"build the ``visualization_marker_tutorials`` package. The ``-b`` option "
"selects the branch for this ROS distribution:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:65
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros2_ws/src\n"
"$ git clone -b rolling https://github.com/ros-visualization/"
"visualization_tutorials.git\n"
"$ cd ~/ros2_ws\n"
"$ colcon build --packages-select visualization_marker_tutorials"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:72
msgid ""
"If your workspace is not ``~/ros2_ws``, use your workspace path instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:75
msgid "2 Start the marker publisher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:77
msgid ""
"Open a new terminal, source your workspace overlay, and run ``basic_shapes``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:79
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros2_ws\n"
"$ source install/setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run visualization_marker_tutorials basic_shapes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:85
msgid ""
"Leave this terminal running. The node publishes a new shape about once a "
"second, replacing the previous marker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:88
msgid ""
"The source for that node is `basic_shapes.cpp <https://github.com/ros-"
"visualization/visualization_tutorials/blob/rolling/"
"visualization_marker_tutorials/src/basic_shapes.cpp>`__. You do not need to "
"edit it for this tutorial."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:92
msgid "3 Start RViz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:94
msgid "Open a new terminal and start RViz:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:96
msgid "$ ros2 run rviz2 rviz2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:100
msgid ""
"You do not need the workspace overlay in this terminal. ``rviz2`` comes from "
"your ROS installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:103
msgid ""
"When RViz starts for the first time, you should see a window like the "
"following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:107
msgid ""
"The large black area is the 3D view. It is empty until a display has "
"something to draw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:110
msgid ""
"On the left is the **Displays** list. It already contains **Global Options** "
"and a **Grid**. **Fixed Frame** defaults to ``map``. **Global Status** may "
"show a warning because the sample publisher does not publish transforms. "
"That is expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:116
msgid ""
"On the right is the **Views** panel. If it is hidden, open it from the "
"**Panels** menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:120
msgid "4 Set the fixed frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:122
msgid ""
"A physical robot operates within a three-dimensional world. The fixed frame "
"in RViz is the reference frame, the world in which the visualized robot "
"operates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:125
msgid ""
"In the **Displays** list, expand **Global Options** if needed, then set "
"**Fixed Frame** to ``my_frame``. Type the name without a leading slash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:128
msgid ""
"The marker node publishes messages in the ``my_frame`` frame, and that name "
"is the fixed frame. The sample code sets the frame as ``/my_frame``, with a "
"leading slash, but frame names in ROS 2 do not start with a slash, so RViz "
"removes it. It does not publish transforms, so RViz must use that same frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:132
msgid ""
"If **Fixed Frame** stays at ``map``, the marker will not show in the 3D view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:135
msgid "5 Add a Marker display"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:137
msgid ""
"The Marker display can show shapes that a node publishes as "
"``visualization_msgs/msg/Marker`` messages. RViz does not need to know the "
"meaning of marker data ahead of time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:140
msgid ""
"The **Displays** list in RViz defines which different elements are included "
"in the visualization. You need to subscribe to the marker messages to "
"include them in the 3D view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:143
msgid "At the bottom of the **Displays** list, select **Add**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:147
msgid ""
"The **Create visualization** dialog opens on the **By display type** tab:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:151
msgid ""
"Select the **By topic** tab. It lists the topics that are currently being "
"published, with the displays that can show each one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:153
msgid ""
"Under ``/visualization_marker``, select **Marker**, then select **OK**. RViz "
"adds a Marker display that subscribes to ``/visualization_marker``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:156
msgid ""
"If ``/visualization_marker`` is not listed, check that ``basic_shapes`` is "
"still running in the other terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:158
msgid ""
"You should now see a green marker at the origin that changes shape about "
"once every second: cube, sphere, arrow, then cylinder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:163
msgid ""
"The Marker display status should be **OK**. **Global Status** can stay at "
"**Warn** because nothing is publishing transforms. If the Marker status is a "
"warning or error, expand the Marker entry and check that the topic is ``/"
"visualization_marker`` and that **Fixed Frame** is ``my_frame``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:168
msgid "6 Change the view"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:170
msgid ""
"The **Views** panel controls how RViz moves the camera and how it projects "
"the 3D scene. Each camera type combines a control scheme with a projection, "
"either perspective or orthographic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:175
msgid "To see how the camera types differ, try the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:177
msgid ""
"In the **Views** panel, check the **Type** list. The default camera type is "
"**Orbit**. The camera rotates around a focal point and always looks at that "
"point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:180
msgid ""
"In the **Type** list, select **FPS**. The camera now looks around from its "
"own position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:182
msgid ""
"In the **Type** list, select **TopDownOrtho**. The camera looks down the "
"fixed-frame Z axis. Objects do not get smaller with distance, because the "
"projection is orthographic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:186
msgid ""
"The **Save** button on the **Views** panel stores a named view, including "
"the camera type, pose, and target frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:191
msgid "7 Move the camera"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:193
msgid ""
"Use the **Orbit** camera type to rotate, pan, and zoom around the marker in "
"the 3D view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:195
msgid "In the **Views** panel, in the **Type** list, select **Orbit**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:197
msgid "On the toolbar, select the **Move Camera** tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:199
msgid "On first start, **Interact** may already be selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:201
msgid "The keyboard shortcut is :kbd:`m`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:203
msgid ""
"When **Move Camera** is selected, clicking in the 3D view moves the camera "
"using the current view type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:205
msgid "RViz shows the focal point as a small disc while you move the camera:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:209
msgid "In the 3D view, try the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:211
msgid "**Left mouse button**: Click and drag to rotate around the focal point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:212
msgid ""
"**Middle mouse button**, or :kbd:`Shift` and **left mouse button**: Click "
"and drag to move the focal point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:213
msgid ""
"**Right mouse button**: Click and drag to zoom. Drag up to zoom in, and down "
"to zoom out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:215
msgid "**Scroll wheel**: Zoom in and out of the focal point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:217
msgid ""
"The status bar also summarizes these controls when **Move Camera** is "
"selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:219
msgid ""
"Rotate, pan, and zoom until you can see the changing marker clearly against "
"the grid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:222
msgid "8 Clean up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:224
msgid ""
"When you are done, stop ``basic_shapes`` and RViz by pressing :kbd:`Ctrl+C` "
"in each of their terminals. You can also close the terminals instead."
msgstr ""

