#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:240
msgid "What is RViz?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:241
msgid ""
"RViz is a 3D visualizer for ROS. It draws data from your system in a 3D "
"view, using displays such as Grid, Marker, and RobotModel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:244
msgid "Why do I set the fixed frame to ``my_frame``?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:245
msgid ""
"The sample publisher puts its markers in the ``my_frame`` frame. It does not "
"publish transforms, so RViz must use that same frame as **Fixed Frame**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:248
msgid "Why is the 3D view black or empty?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:249
msgid ""
"RViz has nothing to draw until you add a display that is receiving data. "
"Start ``basic_shapes``, set **Fixed Frame** to ``my_frame``, and add a "
"Marker display on ``/visualization_marker``. If **Fixed Frame** is still "
"``map``, the marker will not appear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:253
msgid "How do I rotate, pan, or zoom the 3D view?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:254
msgid ""
"Select the **Move Camera** tool (shortcut :kbd:`m`). **Interact** may be "
"selected when RViz starts. Keep the **Orbit** view, then, in the 3D view, "
"use the mouse. Left-drag rotates, middle-drag or :kbd:`Shift`-left-drag "
"moves the focal point, and right-drag or the scroll wheel zooms."
msgstr ""
